{% include 'DGlSyntax.jinja' %}

For ODEs controlled by Angel, the weakest precondition computation involves finding the largest set of initial states from which the system can evolve and satisfy the postcondition while respecting the constraint Q.

For ODEs controlled by Demon, the weakest precondition computation involves finding the largest set of initial states from which the system can evolve and satisfy the postcondition while respecting the constraint Q *regardless of how long the system is run, which is outside our control*. We cannot assume anything about duration except that Q must be satisfied throughout every permissible duration.

